Title: Um modelo de jogo cooperativo sobre os efeitos da corrupção no gasto público
Abstract: This paper analyzes the growth of the population's perception regarding to corruption crimes around the world, assuming the hypothesis of economic coordination among public managers to elaborate strokes against the state. Using samples of international public spending, containing 22 countries and dynamic panel models, it is concluded that exist correlation to a more efficient partition between countries for defense spending. In addition to this observation, it appears that there is correlation between the corrupt behavior of policymakers for spending on public services, environmental protection and community works.
Creation-Date: 2014-10-06
Number: 40/2014
